    "title_en": "First observation of the decay $D_{s1}(2460)^{+} \\to D_{s}^{*+}γ$ and measurement of the branching-fraction ratio $\\mathcal{B}[D_{s1}(2460)^{+} \\to D_{s}^{*+} γ]/\\mathcal{B}[D_{s1}(2460)^{+} \\to D_{s}^{+} γ]$",
    "abstract_en": "We report the first observation of the radiative decay $D_{s1}(2460)^{+} \\to D_{s}^{*+} γ$ with a significance greater than 10 standard deviations. The signal is found in $e^{+}e^{-} \\to c\\bar{c}$ production using data samples with integrated luminosities of 980 and 572~$\\mathrm{fb}^{-1}$ collected by the Belle and Belle~II detectors operating at the KEKB and SuperKEKB asymmetric-energy $e^{+}e^{-}$ colliders, respectively. The branching-fraction ratio $\\mathcal{B}[D_{s1}(2460)^{+} \\to D_{s}^{*+} γ]/\\mathcal{B}[D_{s1}(2460)^{+} \\to D_{s}^{+} γ]$ is measured to be $0.74 \\pm 0.05 ({\\rm stat.}) \\pm 0.06 ({\\rm syst.)}$. This result helps discriminate between different theoretical models regarding the internal structure of the charm-strange meson $D_{s1}(2460)^{+}$.",
